        - Tab 2: AR0234CS 센서 & I2C 제어 (Double Buffering Register Simulator & Context Switching)
        - Tab 3: UVC 토폴로지 & V4L2 매핑 (Topology Nodes, Control Requests, IOCTL Code Generator)
        - Tab 4: 대역폭 & USB 페이로드 분석기 (Dynamic Chart.js Bandwidth Calculator, wMaxPacketSize Shift Decoder, UVC Payload Header Inspector)
        - Tab 5: 글로벌 셔터 & 트리거 시뮬레이터 (Canvas Motion Artifacts Comparison, Hardware Trigger Pulsed/Sync-Sink Timing & Strobe Delay)
     WHY THIS STRUCTURE: Converts a dense 8-section hardware protocol document into logical, interactive engineering workflows. Developers can simulate hardware timing, test register changes, verify Linux kernel mappings, and inspect bandwidth bottlenecks dynamically. -->

<!-- Visualization & Content Choices:
     - Protocol Stack: Interactive 5-level stacked visualizer -> Goal: Understand end-to-end signal path -> Method: Styled HTML/Tailwind + JS detailed drawer -> Justification: Replaces static text with clickable hierarchy.
     - Bandwidth Bottlenecks: Dynamic Bar Chart -> Goal: Compare YUY2 vs MJPEG vs USB 2.0/3.0 bandwidth limits -> Method: Chart.js Canvas -> Interaction: Dynamic sliders for resolution/FPS -> Justification: Instant visual proof of why USB 2.0 requires MJPEG for 1080p60.
     - Rolling vs Global Shutter: Interactive Animation -> Goal: Demonstrate geometric distortion & partial flash -> Method: HTML5 Canvas -> Interaction: Speed control & mode toggle -> Justification: Directly demonstrates the key selling point of global shutter.
     - UVC Payload Header & Register Double Buffering: Step-by-step interactive simulators -> Method: HTML/JS logic controls -> Confirming NO SVG / NO Mermaid JS. -->

<!-- CONFIRMATION: NO SVG graphics used. NO Mermaid JS used. -->

